WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.818 --> 01:30.738
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.657 --> 01:33.992
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.868 --> 01:35.911
Black Jack.

01:47.353 --> 01:48.603
Let's see...

01:48.809 --> 01:49.562
Good.

01:50.343 --> 01:51.950
And...

01:55.438 --> 01:56.438
Oh, yeah...

01:59.490 --> 02:00.865
Don't look!

02:00.945 --> 02:01.945
Jeez!

02:03.398 --> 02:04.535
Transmit.

02:04.953 --> 02:06.621
I always wonder,

02:06.872 --> 02:08.873
who it is that you are always sending mail to?

02:09.416 --> 02:11.123
It's a secret.

02:11.585 --> 02:15.380
Hey, Doc, why don't you get a cell phone?

02:15.381 --> 02:16.881
I want to send you mail.

02:16.882 --> 02:17.949
Mail?

02:18.258 --> 02:21.094
But you live with me, so you can talk to me anytime.

02:21.095 --> 02:25.223
But there are some things you just
can't tell a person face to face!

02:25.224 --> 02:26.654
Things you can't tell someone face to face?

02:27.393 --> 02:28.267
Like what?

02:28.268 --> 02:31.396
Geez, you don't understand how ladies feel!

02:32.022 --> 02:33.375
No, I don't.

02:33.857 --> 02:38.528
Besides, cell phones can cause
medical equipment to malfunction.

02:38.695 --> 02:40.029
I will never get one!

02:41.323 --> 02:43.741
Ohmigewdness!

02:45.536 --> 02:48.746
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "Hello CQ"

02:45.536 --> 02:48.746
Friendship By Mail

02:49.915 --> 02:52.348
Hello CQ! How are you, Tom?

02:55.295 --> 02:56.921
Playing baseball, like always.

02:57.506 --> 02:59.173
Bottom of the ninth, with two players out.

02:59.208 --> 03:00.091
Bases are loaded.

03:00.259 --> 03:02.051
And I stepped into the box.

03:02.886 --> 03:04.303
The count is one two.

03:04.471 --> 03:06.597
The pitcher threw inside.

03:09.852 --> 03:12.269
The ball flew way over the left fence!

03:12.604 --> 03:14.355
I hit a huge home run to bring us from behind!

03:15.899 --> 03:19.694
That's great! I wished I could have seen it, Jun.

03:19.945 --> 03:22.280
Tom, so how are things going on your end?- -

03:22.281 --> 03:23.990
It's the same as usual.

03:24.158 --> 03:26.826
I ride horseback every day as I chase after stray sheep.

03:26.910 --> 03:29.266
Oh, no, I need to get to work.

03:29.663 --> 03:30.872
Bye, CQ!

03:30.914 --> 03:32.248
Bye bye, CQ!

03:35.919 --> 03:40.631
Jun-chan, were you chatting with your usual friend again?

03:40.632 --> 03:42.008
Yeah.

03:42.217 --> 03:45.052
Are you still lying to him about playing baseball,

03:45.637 --> 03:48.055
even though you can't play sports
because of your-sickness?

03:48.473 --> 03:51.058
Someday, this will cause you trouble.

03:51.059 --> 03:52.393
Leave me alone!

03:52.769 --> 03:54.228
He'll never know.

03:54.271 --> 03:56.230
He is in New Zealand.

03:56.940 --> 04:02.267
I want to forget the fact that I can't run,
at least when I'm chatting online.

04:13.707 --> 04:15.917
Pinoco-chan, you were so late.

04:15.918 --> 04:18.002
I was waiting for you for such a long time.

04:18.128 --> 04:20.964
I sent you a message that I'd be late.

04:21.089 --> 04:22.048
See?

04:23.699 --> 04:25.711
You have the wrong address!

04:26.053 --> 04:27.345
See right there?

04:27.346 --> 04:29.055
It's not an "O", it should be a "P".

04:29.056 --> 04:30.473
It should be "Pogo.”

04:30.766 --> 04:33.351
Your address is confusing.

04:33.352 --> 04:34.101
Huh?

04:34.102 --> 04:36.020
But it's true.

04:42.277 --> 04:43.194
Safe!'

04:43.403 --> 04:44.320
Yeah!

04:49.743 --> 04:52.275
Hey, over there, would you get the ball for us?

04:58.502 --> 05:00.628
Hey, are you okay?

05:01.088 --> 05:02.463
I'm fine.

05:02.839 --> 05:03.923
It's okay.

05:03.924 --> 05:04.715
Good.

05:04.841 --> 05:06.342
Hey, what are you doing?

05:06.343 --> 05:08.135
Coming!

05:08.178 --> 05:11.639
It's your fault for making your
doll's name your mail address.

05:12.804 --> 05:13.684
No way.

05:13.684 --> 05:15.602
It's not Pogo's fault.

05:14.893 --> 05:17.640
I don't care if it's Pogo or Pagu!

05:21.191 --> 05:23.192
Hey, are you okay?

05:23.193 --> 05:24.360
Don't touch me.

05:24.486 --> 05:25.861
I'm fine.

05:26.446 --> 05:29.281
I'm trying to help you, so what's the matter?

05:29.282 --> 05:30.324
Are you ill?

05:30.784 --> 05:32.785
Yeah, I am.

05:32.953 --> 05:34.745
What kind?

05:34.746 --> 05:38.416
My Doc can cure any kind of illness.

05:38.498 --> 05:39.041
Right?

05:39.042 --> 05:41.794
Yeah, he cured me too.

05:42.963 --> 05:48.467
I can't be operated on until I'm fully
grown, even by a master surgeon.

05:49.219 --> 05:50.386
Too bad.

05:51.555 --> 05:52.888
How rude.

05:53.014 --> 05:54.306
Pinoco-chan!

05:54.307 --> 05:55.099
Jun!

05:57.602 --> 05:58.394
Jun.

06:00.355 --> 06:02.773
You were watching the baseball game again?

06:04.067 --> 06:04.984
Are they your friends?

06:05.235 --> 06:06.402
No.

06:06.486 --> 06:07.653
They were just gawking.

06:07.654 --> 06:08.070
Jun!

06:08.071 --> 06:10.493
I'm not a gawker!

06:10.824 --> 06:12.074
I'm sorry.

06:12.534 --> 06:14.076
Let's go home.

06:15.120 --> 06:16.468
I can walk on my own!

06:24.087 --> 06:25.713
Welcome home, honey.

06:25.964 --> 06:26.964
Thanks.

06:29.092 --> 06:30.050
Where's Jun?

06:30.260 --> 06:33.012
He shut himself inside his room.

06:33.013 --> 06:34.054
Again?

06:34.055 --> 06:35.391
How troublesome.

06:36.057 --> 06:40.352
Hey honey, couldn't we cure him somehow?

06:40.896 --> 06:45.065
We have to wait until he's old enough to be operated on.

06:47.736 --> 06:49.554
<i>I want to play baseball.</i>

06:50.655 --> 06:54.867
<i>If I wasn't ill, I could run around every day.</i>

06:58.955 --> 07:00.664
Hello CQ, Tom.

07:00.916 --> 07:02.455
Sorry, were you waiting?

07:02.667 --> 07:05.211
No, I just logged on.

07:05.295 --> 07:06.629
What did you do today?

07:07.005 --> 07:07.755
Today?

07:10.342 --> 07:12.092
I played baseball again.

07:13.053 --> 07:14.553
How did it go?

07:15.180 --> 07:17.264
Well, on the bottom of the ninth...

07:19.184 --> 07:23.228
Honey, I really feel bad for him.

07:23.980 --> 07:26.732
He was watching the baseball game at the local field again.

07:27.150 --> 07:30.986
He must want to play baseball just like them.

07:31.613 --> 07:35.824
But they said that it's dangerous to operate
on him until he has the stamina for it.

07:36.088 --> 07:37.088
I know.

07:37.494 --> 07:40.079
But he only has one childhood.

07:40.622 --> 07:42.915
I want to let him do what he wants.

07:43.541 --> 07:46.669
There are children who die at a young ages too.

07:46.986 --> 07:48.118
Don't be selfish.

07:48.546 --> 07:49.380
You're right.

07:49.381 --> 07:50.839
You are absolutely right.

07:52.509 --> 07:57.304
But I heard that a doctor named Black
Jack might be able to do something.

07:57.931 --> 07:59.264
Black Jack?

07:59.265 --> 08:01.809
Yes, he's a master surgeon.

08:02.185 --> 08:06.438
However, he asks for rather outrageous fees.

08:08.316 --> 08:09.483
I ran!

08:09.859 --> 08:12.277
While the outfielders were occupied,
I ran toward home base!

08:14.572 --> 08:16.573
Safe! I was safe!

08:16.616 --> 08:18.242
I made a home run to bring us from behind!

08:18.785 --> 08:20.494
It felt really good.

08:20.745 --> 08:24.498
I wish I could go to your country,
and play baseball with you.

08:24.624 --> 08:26.375
Yeah, I know.

08:27.544 --> 08:31.463
Jun, I might be able to come to Japan soon.

08:32.215 --> 08:34.508
I plan to come there.

08:34.634 --> 08:36.427
Then I can see you.

08:36.469 --> 08:37.970
I'll visit you before I do anything else!

08:38.596 --> 08:39.596
Really?

08:39.597 --> 08:40.389
Yeah.

08:40.557 --> 08:43.952
Hey, can I stay at your place?

08:44.394 --> 08:46.353
Sure, you're always welcome!

08:46.354 --> 08:49.732
Also, I want to see you play baseball.

08:50.734 --> 08:51.859
I know.

08:53.653 --> 08:54.736
What should I do?

08:55.155 --> 08:57.156
Tom is coming to Japan?

08:57.657 --> 09:00.033
And he'd like to see me play baseball?

09:06.207 --> 09:07.332
Tom?

09:10.670 --> 09:12.421
Stop it, Tom!

09:29.527 --> 09:31.903
Jun, how late are you going to sleep in?

09:31.904 --> 09:32.988
I'm coming in.

09:33.406 --> 09:34.281
Jun.

09:34.782 --> 09:35.490
Jun?

09:36.200 --> 09:36.992
What's the matter?

09:36.993 --> 09:38.326
Are you feeling bad?

09:38.369 --> 09:39.035
Jun?

09:39.537 --> 09:40.495
Mom...

09:41.914 --> 09:46.070
Tom is coming to Japan from New Zealand.

09:46.627 --> 09:49.004
Tom? Your online friend?

09:49.130 --> 09:50.297
That's great.

09:50.423 --> 09:51.756
No, it's not!

09:51.882 --> 09:54.384
He said he wants to see me play baseball.

09:54.552 --> 09:57.429
He'll find out that I was lying to him all this time.

09:57.680 --> 09:59.639
He'll call me a liar!

10:00.016 --> 10:03.602
Jun, this is why you should have told him the truth.

10:03.894 --> 10:08.315
Tell him the truth and then apologize to him.

10:08.482 --> 10:09.316
No.

10:09.859 --> 10:11.234
Not even if I die.

10:11.819 --> 10:14.961
I don't want Tom to know that I'm like this.

10:15.406 --> 10:18.325
Jun, but he ill know when he comes to Japan.

10:18.451 --> 10:20.201
So do something about it!

10:20.328 --> 10:22.162
Heal me!

10:23.414 --> 10:25.123
About that, Jun,

10:25.416 --> 10:27.250
I talked with Dad about it yesterday.

10:27.251 --> 10:30.086
I want to have another doctor take a look at you.

10:31.130 --> 10:32.547
Another doctor?

10:38.137 --> 10:39.596
How long has he had this condition?

10:39.889 --> 10:42.766
He was first diagnosed was when he was four.

10:42.808 --> 10:46.419
We visited many hospitals, but
the results were all the same.

10:46.979 --> 10:49.272
So how is Jun?

10:50.316 --> 10:53.818
I can operate on him once he grows up a
little more and has a bit more stamina.

10:53.819 --> 10:55.278
They told you the same thing, didn't they?

10:55.446 --> 10:56.196
Yes.

10:56.614 --> 11:00.075
But I want to let him play baseball!

11:00.868 --> 11:01.993
Baseball?

11:02.578 --> 11:06.122
We can operate on him with a much
lower risk in another five years.

11:06.457 --> 11:10.251
But are you telling me that he wants to play
baseball so much that he can't wait?

11:10.878 --> 11:12.629
Is that what you mean?

11:13.422 --> 11:14.547
What?

11:14.840 --> 11:17.550
If you can't do it why don't you just say you can't?

11:18.302 --> 11:20.720
Doctors are all the same!

11:20.888 --> 11:22.597
They just try to talk big!

11:22.807 --> 11:23.515
Jun!

11:23.516 --> 11:24.849
Damn!

11:24.975 --> 11:26.601
I didn't say I couldn't.

11:27.603 --> 11:31.356
I have succeeded with this type of operation several times.

11:31.527 --> 11:33.983
So can I be cured?

11:34.276 --> 11:37.362
Doctor, please!

11:37.363 --> 11:40.949
I need to be able to play baseball!

11:41.575 --> 11:43.910
Why are you so particular about playing baseball?

11:44.078 --> 11:46.746
Or else, I will be a liar!

11:46.789 --> 11:50.542
It doesn't have to be perfect -- just while Tom is here.

11:51.335 --> 11:53.670
So, Doctor, please!

11:54.213 --> 11:56.131
Doctor!

11:57.091 --> 11:58.133
100,000,000.

11:59.051 --> 12:01.315
I will take 100,000,000 yen for the fee.

12:02.346 --> 12:04.013
100,000,000 yen?

12:04.014 --> 12:05.181
No way...

12:06.308 --> 12:09.352
Mom, do we have 100,000,000 yen?

12:09.353 --> 12:12.105
We could never have that kind of money.

12:14.150 --> 12:15.525
I'm home.

12:15.761 --> 12:16.693
Enough!

12:17.570 --> 12:19.028
Geez!

12:19.109 --> 12:20.614
Wait, Jun!

12:19.822 --> 12:21.447
Oh, Largo, no!

12:22.449 --> 12:25.285
Doctors are all greedy snobs!

12:25.995 --> 12:28.121
Why don't you deal only with rich people?

12:28.998 --> 12:30.331
You!

12:35.462 --> 12:39.290
Hey, Doc, why wouldn't you help him?

12:39.592 --> 12:41.801
I'm not a philanthropist.

12:42.052 --> 12:48.182
Besides, if the patient is not completely serious
about getting well, operating will be useless.

12:54.648 --> 12:57.066
Damn that doctor.

12:58.402 --> 13:00.403
I wish I could get well.

13:06.160 --> 13:08.870
<i>Then I could run freely.</i>

13:13.167 --> 13:16.419
<i>I can't see Tom like this.</i>

13:18.881 --> 13:20.840
Hello CQ, Tom.

13:21.258 --> 13:22.925
Hello CQ, Jun.

13:22.926 --> 13:23.384
How are you?

13:24.428 --> 13:26.141
I looked at the photos you sent me.

13:26.347 --> 13:28.306
You are tall and handsome.

13:28.307 --> 13:30.350
Huh? Tall?

13:30.476 --> 13:32.769
But I only sent a portrait photo.

13:32.895 --> 13:34.520
Oh, that's right.

13:35.022 --> 13:37.899
I'm a little tired from work I did around the ranch.

13:38.734 --> 13:41.401
There's a lot to do around this time
of year when you're raising sheep.

13:42.154 --> 13:45.740
Oh, and a horse from the next ranch escaped,

13:45.741 --> 13:47.867
so I had to catch her on horseback.

13:48.577 --> 13:51.079
I'm good with horses,

13:51.121 --> 13:53.456
and since everyone admires my skill, they ask
me to do things, which keeps me busy.

13:53.916 --> 13:57.502
So they invited me to a barbeque to thank me.

13:57.532 --> 14:02.079
<i>Tom is having so much fun, while
I have so many problems.</i>

13:57.878 --> 13:59.253
It was great!

14:02.845 --> 14:03.477
<i>Dang!</i>

14:04.760 --> 14:07.011
Yeah! Tom is a mean guy.

14:07.805 --> 14:10.160
Break off your friendship with him.

14:10.724 --> 14:13.309
You can have a fight with him,
and then never see him again.

14:13.727 --> 14:15.978
Then you don't have to be a liar.

14:16.105 --> 14:17.772
You don't have to get hurt.

14:17.773 --> 14:19.065
... it was great!

14:19.066 --> 14:21.859
Oh yeah, I finalized the date for my trip to Japan.

14:21.860 --> 14:23.638
I can stay for about three months.

14:25.155 --> 14:25.905
Jun?

14:26.365 --> 14:27.240
Jun?

14:27.533 --> 14:30.243
Oh? Did the line drop?

14:31.662 --> 14:37.014
Tom, I want to end our friendship.

14:38.168 --> 14:39.168
What?!

14:39.545 --> 14:41.337
I want to stop being friends with you.

14:41.755 --> 14:43.375
I don't want to talk to you anymore.

14:43.590 --> 14:46.634
Jun, what are you angry about?

14:46.969 --> 14:49.887
I got tired of your bragging.

14:49.888 --> 14:51.139
No way...

14:51.473 --> 14:53.213
So this is the end for us.

14:53.392 --> 14:56.227
Jun, I'm finally coming to Japan!

14:56.228 --> 14:57.562
I can see you!

14:57.563 --> 14:58.604
This is goodbye.

14:58.605 --> 14:59.522
Wait!

14:59.648 --> 15:02.608
There's something I want you to see and hear.

15:02.734 --> 15:03.901
I don't want to hear it!

15:04.069 --> 15:04.694
Jun!

15:04.820 --> 15:05.736
Jun!

15:05.445 --> 15:07.485
Goodbye

15:08.532 --> 15:09.407
Jun!

15:13.287 --> 15:17.498
Jun, what was that yelling about?

15:17.958 --> 15:22.134
Mom, I ended my friendship with Tom.

15:23.672 --> 15:26.132
He was a good friend...

15:27.220 --> 15:28.476
Leave me alone.

15:29.344 --> 15:30.595
Get out!

15:41.690 --> 15:44.567
Pinoco-chan, your mail didn't reach me again.

15:44.693 --> 15:46.319
That can't be.

15:46.445 --> 15:48.029
Hey, that kid...

15:51.158 --> 15:52.658
Hey!

15:53.201 --> 15:54.712
Throw the ball over here!

16:01.668 --> 16:03.294
Hey! What was that for?

16:04.671 --> 16:07.176
If you're mad, why don't you hit me?

16:08.008 --> 16:08.966
Hit me!

16:08.967 --> 16:09.759
Hey.

16:10.385 --> 16:11.260
What's wrong?

16:12.346 --> 16:14.347
What did you do that for?

16:14.348 --> 16:15.431
It's none of your business!

16:17.601 --> 16:20.019
But don't you love baseball?

16:20.437 --> 16:21.648
I hate it.

16:21.897 --> 16:24.231
It really hurts when the ball hits me.

16:24.232 --> 16:27.753
Sharaku, are you telling me that you've played baseball?

16:28.028 --> 16:28.976
Of course I have!

16:29.056 --> 16:29.820
Liar!

16:29.821 --> 16:32.949
I've never seen you play baseball!

16:33.042 --> 16:34.102
I have!

16:34.275 --> 16:35.201
Honest!

16:35.202 --> 16:36.160
Liar!

16:36.161 --> 16:38.288
Liar! Liar! Liar! Liar!

16:37.454 --> 16:40.039
Quit repeating "liar, liar!"

16:45.629 --> 16:50.413
Why didn't you tell Tom the truth?

16:50.884 --> 16:52.426
How could I tell him?

16:52.844 --> 16:57.098
If I did, he would have hated me.

16:57.182 --> 16:59.058
That's not true.

16:59.267 --> 17:01.769
I think it's worse to be lied to.

17:01.770 --> 17:02.895
He's right.

17:02.979 --> 17:05.022
You're attacking me too!

17:05.148 --> 17:06.941
Just like my mom did!

17:07.192 --> 17:08.140
I've had enough.

17:18.389 --> 17:20.289
Hello C

17:24.751 --> 17:25.626
Tom...

17:27.713 --> 17:29.468
Jun!

17:31.466 --> 17:32.925
What's up, Mom?

17:32.926 --> 17:34.677
Jun, the doctor will...

17:34.678 --> 17:38.055
Dr. Black Jack will operate on you!

17:38.598 --> 17:39.890
But how?

17:39.891 --> 17:40.975
We don't have the money.

17:41.017 --> 17:42.893
But he said he'll drop the fee down to a hundred yen!

17:43.270 --> 17:45.271
Huh? A hundred yen?

17:45.939 --> 17:48.566
He's mocking us.

17:49.443 --> 17:50.818
Were you surprised?

17:51.445 --> 17:54.447
I told your story to a company president,

17:54.448 --> 17:58.367
and he wanted to pay for your surgery.

17:58.827 --> 18:00.453
A rich president?

18:00.704 --> 18:03.831
Why would a total stranger want to help me?

18:04.124 --> 18:08.252
This president lost his father when he was young, and
consequently succeeded his father's place in the company.

18:08.962 --> 18:13.215
But due to an optical accident, he lost
his eyesight when he was a child.

18:14.009 --> 18:18.095
He heard about me, and came to Japan,

18:18.221 --> 18:21.390
but for some reason, he said he had lost
interest in getting his sight back.

18:21.808 --> 18:24.768
So he no longer needs the money to pay for it.

18:25.812 --> 18:27.855
I talked to him about you,

18:28.273 --> 18:31.609
including the fact that you lost a friendship in order
to hide the fact that you can't play baseball.

18:31.735 --> 18:34.278
How do you know that?

18:34.321 --> 18:35.738
Because of me!

18:35.989 --> 18:36.739
You?

18:36.740 --> 18:39.283
I told him everything.

18:40.035 --> 18:45.080
This president said that he will be financially responsible
for the surgery to make up for your lost friendship.

18:45.832 --> 18:48.167
He said for me to cure you instead of him.

18:48.543 --> 18:50.002
But why?

18:50.003 --> 18:52.463
Why would he want that?

18:52.672 --> 18:53.964
Why?

18:54.090 --> 18:56.258
Why don't you ask him yourself?

18:57.177 --> 18:57.927
Come in.

19:01.014 --> 19:05.100
He is the president of a wool textile
company, Mr. Thomas Morrison.

19:07.729 --> 19:11.732
Can you imagine how upset I was, Jun?

19:15.028 --> 19:16.695
Hello, CQ.

19:17.822 --> 19:18.781
<i>Could it be...</i>

19:19.991 --> 19:21.617
Is that you, Tom?

19:23.036 --> 19:24.828
Yes, it's me.

19:24.871 --> 19:26.580
I arrived in Japan yesterday.

19:26.998 --> 19:29.875
It's really you.

19:29.960 --> 19:34.251
Jun, I've been lying to you by telling you that I could see.

19:34.965 --> 19:35.881
Please forgive me.

19:36.216 --> 19:37.925
I've been lying too.

19:38.259 --> 19:39.134
I'm sorry.

19:39.344 --> 19:42.846
But, Tom, are you serious about not
wanting to get your sight back?

19:42.973 --> 19:46.787
I was in a rush to get the surgery done so I could see you.

19:47.227 --> 19:50.312
But now that I lost my friendship with you, it's useless.

19:50.730 --> 19:53.524
Use the money to get yourself healed.

19:53.525 --> 19:56.402
Tom, please don't talk like that.

19:56.861 --> 19:59.279
Please get your sight back.

19:59.364 --> 20:05.041
Jun, if we use the money for Tom's
operation, I can't work on you.

20:05.662 --> 20:08.247
Are you sure, as this means you will
not be able to play baseball?

20:09.374 --> 20:10.958
Oh, come on!

20:10.959 --> 20:12.418
What does it matter as long as you get better!

20:12.794 --> 20:14.920
Then you can finally play baseball like you wanted.

20:15.130 --> 20:16.807
Don't be shy, Jun!

20:16.854 --> 20:17.854
I...

20:18.466 --> 20:21.205
I'm okay with not being able to play baseball!

20:24.055 --> 20:26.056
I didn't want to not be friends.

20:26.224 --> 20:29.226
Tom, I still want to be your friend!

20:30.103 --> 20:32.479
So, Tom, please get your sight back!

20:32.480 --> 20:34.314
And see my face!

20:34.691 --> 20:38.277
Doctor, I can be operated on in a few years.

20:38.403 --> 20:40.320
But that's not the case for Tom, right?

20:40.572 --> 20:42.781
Please work on Tom's eyes!

20:42.907 --> 20:47.536
Jun, I have been lonely ever since
I lost the light in my eyes.

20:47.746 --> 20:51.329
But I finally found a new friend: you.

20:54.127 --> 20:58.315
You are a priceless friend to me, Jun.

20:58.798 --> 20:59.465
Tom...

21:01.968 --> 21:04.303
Doctor, please work on Jun.

21:04.304 --> 21:07.181
No, please work on Tom.

21:07.599 --> 21:11.059
Oh, boy, I hate it when people can't decide.

21:11.686 --> 21:13.896
If you can't decide on your own, it can't be helped.

21:14.856 --> 21:16.315
I'll decide then.

21:21.940 --> 21:23.614
I'll work on both of you.

21:23.823 --> 21:26.283
That's the easiest solution.

21:28.077 --> 21:31.830
Now, which one of you will come in first?

21:32.916 --> 21:36.043
...and transmit.

21:36.085 --> 21:39.421
Hey, Pinoco, are you sending mail again?

21:39.422 --> 21:40.839
Yep.

21:41.758 --> 21:44.384
Seriously, who are you communicating with?

21:44.385 --> 21:45.511
It's a secret.

21:45.720 --> 21:49.139
I'll tell you if you get a cell phone.

21:49.766 --> 21:50.599
No way.

21:51.184 --> 21:52.726
Hello CQ, Tom.

21:52.727 --> 21:54.102
Hello CQ, Jun.

21:54.520 --> 21:56.063
How's baseball going?

21:56.105 --> 21:57.981
I'm still chasing after the balls.

21:58.107 --> 21:59.066
It's okay.

21:59.067 --> 22:00.481
You can do it.

22:01.069 --> 22:02.110
Thank you.

22:02.153 --> 22:05.239
By the way, have you finalized the
dates for your next visit to Japan?

22:07.120 --> 22:19.075
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.120 --> 22:19.075
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.193 --> 22:24.192
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.193 --> 22:24.192
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.761 --> 22:31.230
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.761 --> 22:31.230
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.774 --> 22:37.232
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.774 --> 22:37.232
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.836 --> 22:40.321
being heated up by you,

22:37.836 --> 22:40.321
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.530 --> 22:48.307
so much that I change color

22:40.530 --> 22:48.307
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.392 --> 23:00.161
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.392 --> 23:00.161
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.369 --> 23:12.100
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.369 --> 23:12.100
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.340 --> 23:23.691
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.340 --> 23:23.691
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.877 --> 23:28.798
I couldn't be happier

23:23.877 --> 23:28.798
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:29.026 --> 23:33.960
How does it taste?

23:29.026 --> 23:33.959
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.097 --> 24:15.102
Good Luck, Kowa Clinic

23:47.032 --> 23:48.616
Next patient, please.

23:48.617 --> 23:51.410
He's about the only doctor around here.

23:51.411 --> 23:54.622
There's no other doctor who is as skilled and as kind.

23:54.915 --> 23:57.083
Hey, there's a suspicious man out there.

23:57.084 --> 23:59.877
I don't want this!

24:04.624 --> 24:05.977
You are truly great.

24:06.510 --> 24:11.097
You are admired by all of the villagers.

24:11.431 --> 24:14.350
Next Karte - Good Luck, Kowa Clinic.

24:16.144 --> 24:17.640
Karte NG...

24:19.823 --> 24:21.450
That's not true...

24:22.113 --> 24:22.927
Pinoco-chan.

24:22.927 --> 24:23.582
Cut! Cut!
